      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Mauryan Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chandragupta Maurya founded the empire and ruled from 322–298 BCE.",
        "Bindusara succeeded Chandragupta Maurya, ruling from 298–273 BCE.",
        "Ashoka the Great reigned from 273–232 BCE and established Ashoka's Dhamma following the Kalinga War.",
        "The empire developed robust administrative and economic structures.",
        "Mauryan Art and Architecture advanced significantly during this era."
